    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end. The endpoint is the single `POST /api/owners` create pipeline (tests read the value back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), so `title` had to be accepted on input, persisted, and used to compose the read-only `salutation` on output.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 the DTOs are generated from this at build time:\n   - Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema (\u2192 `OwnerFieldsDto`).\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema (\u2192 `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter so the value survives POST \u2192 GET.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`); tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`. Also fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` positional seed inserts (added a `NULL` for the new column).\n\n4. **Salutation helper** (`rest/function/owner/Salutation.java`) \u2014 `of(title, lastName)` returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`, matching the existing helper-class pattern.\n\n5. **OwnerMapper** \u2014 mapped `salutation` via the helper. `title` maps automatically (same name) in `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` used by `BuildOwner`.\n\n6. **ApplyOwner** (PUT path) \u2014 also applies `title` for consistency, so updates keep the field editable.\n\nThe test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and it's the only test in the suite.",
